| Detection Metadata                                                                    |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Detection Name    : Process Injection Indicators                                      |
| Detection ID      : DET-006                                                           |
| MITRE Tactic      : Defense Evasion / Privilege Escalation                           |
| MITRE Technique   : T1055 — Process Injection                                        |
| Severity          : Critical                                                          |
| Data Sources      : Sysmon Event 8 (CreateRemoteThread), Sysmon Event 10             |

================================================================================
PRIMARY QUERY — CreateRemoteThread Detection
================================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
EventID=8
NOT SourceImage IN (
    "*\\svchost.exe",
    "*\\csrss.exe",
    "*\\wininit.exe",
    "*\\lsass.exe",
    "*\\MsMpEng.exe",
    "*\\SecurityHealthService.exe"
)
| eval detection="CreateRemoteThread — Process Injection Indicator"
| eval mitre="T1055"
| eval severity="Critical"
| eval high_value_target=if(
    TargetImage IN ("*\\svchost.exe","*\\explorer.exe","*\\lsass.exe","*\\winlogon.exe"),
    "HIGH RISK — injection into privileged target",
    "REVIEW — cross-process thread creation"
  )
| table _time, ComputerName, User, SourceImage, TargetImage, StartAddress, StartFunction, high_value_target
| sort -_time

================================================================================
KNOWN FALSE POSITIVES
================================================================================
- AV/EDR agents using hook injection (add to exclusion list after verification)
- Debuggers and profiling tools (Visual Studio, WinDbg)
- Some .NET and Java runtimes
